The locked pricing formula for **Bargain Drop** is:

$$\text{Price} = \lceil \text{USD\_cost} \times \text{multiplier} \times 1.4234 \rceil - 0.05$$

### Key Parameters:
* **FX Rate:** `1.4234`
* **Rounding:** Always ends in `.95` (`ceil(...) - 0.05`)
* **Compare-At Price:** `null`

### Tier Multipliers:
| Base USD Cost | Multiplier |
| :--- | :--- |
| **< $10.00** | `3.2x` |
| **$10.00 â $15.00** | `2.8x` |
| **$15.01 â $22.00** | `2.5x` |
| **$22.01 â $30.00** | `2.2x` |
| **$30.01 â $60.00** | `1.9x` |
| **> $60.00** | `1.7x` |

---

### Implementation (JavaScript)

```javascript
function calculateOptimizedPrice(usdCost) {
  let multiplier;

  if (usdCost < 10) {
    multiplier = 3.2;
  } else if (usdCost <= 15) {
    multiplier = 2.8;
  } else if (usdCost <= 22) {
    multiplier = 2.5;
  } else if (usdCost <= 30) {
    multiplier = 2.2;
  } else if (usdCost <= 60) {
    multiplier = 1.9;
  } else {
    multiplier = 1.7;
  }

  const fxRate = 1.4234;
  const rawPrice = usdCost * multiplier * fxRate;
  const finalPrice = Math.ceil(rawPrice) - 0.05;

  return {
    price: Number(finalPrice.toFixed(2)),
    compare_at_price: null
  };
}
```

